WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.397
The holiday season for many is a time of celebration, generosity, and tradition.

00:00:04.397 --> 00:00:08.397
For some, there is a mascot who effortlessly exemplifies all of these qualities,

00:00:08.397 --> 00:00:11.267
and his name is the Hebrew Hammer. And he's awesome.

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:14.550
-[Hebrew Hammer] Happy Hanukkah Maccabee.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:17.520
-[Kid] Thanks Hammer!

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:21.706
But for others, there is Santa Claus, a jolly fat man who employs slave labor

00:00:21.738 --> 00:00:24.222
and breaks into people's houses in the middle of the night.

00:00:24.276 --> 00:00:27.702
But those who are initiated may be surprised to learn that Santa is actually

00:00:27.756 --> 00:00:28.738
the good version.

00:00:28.834 --> 00:00:32.966
Many pop culture icons have another side to them, a shadow, a yang to their yin.

00:00:32.988 --> 00:00:34.978
Superman has Bizarro.

00:00:35.074 --> 00:00:36.370
Spider-man has Venom.

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:38.038
Link has Dark Link.

00:00:38.124 --> 00:00:40.770
Even Airrack has an evil twin named Brent Rivera.

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:44.186
But in the case of old Saint Nick, his shadow is not an opponent, but sort

00:00:44.208 --> 00:00:44.950
of an ally.

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:48.506
If you want to hear how the ancient entity known as Krampus tortured a

00:00:48.528 --> 00:00:52.766
generation of naughty kids and how one family in 2015 reawakened him like

00:00:52.788 --> 00:00:55.840
never before, stick around to the end of this video.

00:00:55.840 --> 00:01:01.751
♪ Metal Music ♪

00:01:01.751 --> 00:01:04.094
Welcome to ho-ho-Horror History.

00:01:04.212 --> 00:01:06.582
I can truly never forgive myself for that joke.

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:09.854
Earlier this year, I made a Horror History episode on Sam, the Halloween mascot

00:01:09.902 --> 00:01:13.566
from director Michael Dougherty's 2007 horror anthology Trick r Treat,

00:01:13.598 --> 00:01:16.758
where I also mentioned another holiday tradition horror film that

00:01:16.764 --> 00:01:19.910
Dougherty had directed: his 2015 film Krampus.

00:01:20.181 --> 00:01:24.090
♪ Toys in every store ♪

00:01:24.737 --> 00:01:26.966
In the first video, I talked about how Sam's role was to

00:01:26.988 --> 00:01:30.066
preserve ancient holiday traditions, punishing those who break the holidays rules.

00:01:30.098 --> 00:01:32.774
So Krampus, in a way, is a spiritual successor.

00:01:32.822 --> 00:01:36.058
But instead of enforcing traditions of Celtic folklore, Krampus hails from

00:01:36.064 --> 00:01:37.734
ancient Alpine and Nordic legends. 

00:01:37.782 --> 00:01:41.242
Typically depicted as a horned goat demon hybrid, Krampus is sometimes

00:01:41.296 --> 00:01:44.550
covered in black fur, while at other times taking a more human appearance.

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:47.866
He's often seen covered in chains and sporting a bundle of birch branches,

00:01:47.898 --> 00:01:50.286
which are used to imprison and swat misbehaving children.

00:01:50.388 --> 00:01:53.674
He can sometimes be seen with a bundle or sack, much like Santa Claus himself.

00:01:53.722 --> 00:01:56.618
But instead of using it to distribute toys, it's usually filled

00:01:56.634 --> 00:01:58.850
with bad kids so he can transport them to hell.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:02.206
Capturing children inside of his sack is one of the many parallels

00:02:02.238 --> 00:02:02.782
he shares with Sam.

00:02:02.846 --> 00:02:06.214
But to understand Krampus and to stay off his naughty list, I'm going to go

00:02:06.252 --> 00:02:07.398
over his entire history.

00:02:07.484 --> 00:02:10.470
So let's take it back to the earliest winter celebration.

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:11.804
(IMPACT)

00:02:11.804 --> 00:02:14.951
♪ Haunting Holiday Music ♪

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:19.202
While the date of Krampus's origin has seemingly been lost time, the holiday

00:02:19.266 --> 00:02:22.854
traditions that he represents ironically trace back even before Christmas,

00:02:22.902 --> 00:02:26.687
and Krampus only became associated with the holiday once it became widespread.

00:02:26.687 --> 00:02:28.326
It's believed that the Romans were one of the biggest

00:02:28.358 --> 00:02:31.098
celebrators of the winter solstice, the longest night of the year in the

00:02:31.104 --> 00:02:31.942
northern hemisphere.

00:02:32.006 --> 00:02:35.566
The most popular holiday on the ancient Roman calendar was Saturnalia,

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:38.110
A celebration of Saturn, the God of agriculture and time.

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:41.114
As with many ancient traditions, this was all about farming rituals.

00:02:41.162 --> 00:02:43.646
People would offer gifts to the gods in hopes that it would bless their

00:02:43.668 --> 00:02:46.286
winter sowing season, which is basically just when it was time to get the

00:02:46.308 --> 00:02:49.626
seeds in the cold ground, as described in the song Sowing Season by Brand New.

00:02:49.658 --> 00:02:52.557
I'd have to give up my emo card if I didn't mention that.

00:02:52.557 --> 00:02:55.760
Saturnalia started as just one day, but then they just said, screw it,

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:56.582
let's just make it a whole week.

00:02:56.636 --> 00:02:59.474
So it lasted from December 17th to December 25th.

00:02:59.522 --> 00:03:02.518
It's a lot like how Christmas in America lasts several months before the

00:03:02.524 --> 00:03:04.162
actual day, which is super annoying.

00:03:04.226 --> 00:03:07.490
So that may potentially be the origin of December gift giving tradition.

00:03:07.570 --> 00:03:10.293
Saturnalia was also a time to let loose with food and drinks,

00:03:10.293 --> 00:03:11.202
just like every holiday.

00:03:11.266 --> 00:03:14.102
And businesses and schools were closed so that everyone could participate,

00:03:14.166 --> 00:03:15.306
and I do mean everyone.

00:03:15.408 --> 00:03:18.922
It was seen as a time that all social classes could come together and celebrate.

00:03:18.922 --> 00:03:21.322
Even slaves were given temporary freedom during this time.

00:03:21.376 --> 00:03:24.506
It seems that this tradition is kind of reflected in Krampus, which features

00:03:24.538 --> 00:03:27.674
the mom, Sarah Engel, and her family coming together to celebrate Christmas

00:03:27.722 --> 00:03:29.550
with her less well off sister's family.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:31.027
–[LINDA] They got even more stuff.

00:03:31.027 --> 00:03:33.102
–[HOWARD] Man, how come rich people get all the free sh*t?

00:03:33.236 --> 00:03:36.314
Part of the Saturnalia tradition was the celebration of the God Mithra,

00:03:36.362 --> 00:03:37.882
which fell on December 25th.

00:03:37.946 --> 00:03:40.754
There are people, I'm not going to say who, but they are out there who believe that

00:03:40.792 --> 00:03:44.126
when the Roman-Catholic Church selected the date, December 25th, for Christmas,

00:03:44.158 --> 00:03:47.995
their goal was to replace the Pagan pre-Christianity rituals.

00:03:47.995 --> 00:03:50.062
The Christians are vehemently opposed to this theory.

00:03:50.126 --> 00:03:52.626
If you ask the Christian scholars how often they think about the Roman Empire,

00:03:52.658 --> 00:03:55.350
they'll get nervous and say, I don't know what you're talking about,

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:58.274
but it's true that Jesus' actual date of birth is unknown.

00:03:58.322 --> 00:03:59.526
They will admit that much.

00:03:59.628 --> 00:04:01.750
Christmas is just the day that they celebrate it.

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:03.622
But enough with all of this Roman crap.

00:04:03.686 --> 00:04:06.410
Krampus is clearly a German name, so let's get to that part.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:10.086
Krampus is indeed German, most likely named after the German word krampen,

00:04:10.118 --> 00:04:10.934
which means claw.

00:04:10.982 --> 00:04:13.966
This name is fitting for the character because Krampus is often described as

00:04:13.988 --> 00:04:17.166
a frightening horned creature with sharp claws reflecting its menacing and

00:04:17.188 --> 00:04:18.138
beastly appearance.

00:04:18.234 --> 00:04:22.026
I saw some sources, like Encyclopedia Britannica, claiming that Krampus

00:04:22.058 --> 00:04:24.858
is the son of Hel, the underworld goddess from Norse mythology.

00:04:24.954 --> 00:04:27.678
However, there's no mention of Krampus in Norse mythology.

00:04:27.774 --> 00:04:30.642
It's much more likely that he comes from Alpine folklore, especially

00:04:30.696 --> 00:04:34.402
considering the German name and Austrian traditions that were connected to Krampus.

00:04:34.402 --> 00:04:36.034
Krampus is said to be a counterpart to St. Nicholas,

00:04:36.072 --> 00:04:38.302
who was born in the year 270 CE.

00:04:38.366 --> 00:04:41.654
So it's likely that lore wise Krampus would come into existence around that time.

00:04:41.692 --> 00:04:43.845
While St. Nicholas was a Christian bishop known

00:04:43.845 --> 00:04:45.826
for his kindness and generosity towards children,

00:04:45.826 --> 00:04:48.198
Krampus was the opposite, punishing children who

00:04:48.204 --> 00:04:49.382
misbehaved throughout the year.

00:04:49.436 --> 00:04:53.236
St. Nicholas's followers began to celebrate a feast day in his honor on December 6th,

00:04:53.236 --> 00:04:55.142
during which gift giving became a tradition.

00:04:55.206 --> 00:04:59.226
So Krampus, not to be outdone, got his own holiday on December 5th,

00:04:59.248 --> 00:05:00.150
the eve of St. Nick's feast.

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:03.418
This would be known as Krampusnacht or simply Krampus Night.

00:05:03.504 --> 00:05:06.002
Legend says that both St. Nicholas and Krampus

00:05:06.002 --> 00:05:09.175
would arrive in the evening on December 5th, with St. Nicholas rewarding

00:05:09.175 --> 00:05:11.534
the good kids with presents and Krampus punishing the bad ones with

00:05:11.572 --> 00:05:14.654
chains and his birch branches, even collecting the worst of them

00:05:14.692 --> 00:05:15.678
to drag them to hell.

00:05:15.764 --> 00:05:18.594
Which is a way better behavior motivator than simply the threat of getting

00:05:18.632 --> 00:05:19.534
coal in your stocking.

00:05:19.582 --> 00:05:22.546
If any of you have kids or even younger siblings, I think it's time to start

00:05:22.546 --> 00:05:25.290
telling them about Krampus because this generation is getting

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:26.180
kinda out of control.

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:29.234
– Hey, watch it! (kid spits on her)
– OH! Oh sh--

00:05:29.670 --> 00:05:32.966
But the next Krampusnacht tradition that would emerge would scare even the

00:05:32.988 --> 00:05:36.150
bravest of kids and would become an instant classic.

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:39.506
(IMPACT)

00:05:41.111 --> 00:05:52.427
♪ Krampus Celebration Music ♪

00:05:52.427 --> 00:05:54.101
(ROAR)

00:05:54.101 --> 00:05:56.142
This is Krampuslauf, or Krampus Run,

00:05:56.196 --> 00:05:59.166
A traditional parade started in Austria where the adults dress up in

00:05:59.188 --> 00:06:02.238
realistic Krampus costumes and run through the streets trying to scare the

00:06:02.244 --> 00:06:05.102
children into behaving ahead of the arrival of Krampus and St. Nick.

00:06:05.156 --> 00:06:08.658
According to history.com, Austrian men would get drunk and run through

00:06:08.664 --> 00:06:10.462
the streets dressed as the fearsome creature.

00:06:10.526 --> 00:06:14.878
This account from traveldudes.com mentions 400 gruesome creatures whipping

00:06:14.894 --> 00:06:18.078
the legs of children and stealing hats in freezing cold temperatures.

00:06:18.174 --> 00:06:21.462
Some celebrations also feature women dressing up as Perchta,

00:06:21.516 --> 00:06:23.394
another mythological being in Alpine folklore.

00:06:23.442 --> 00:06:26.690
A goddess who is associated with the winter solstice, just like Krampus.

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:29.686
At first I thought this was just the witch from Snow White, which I guess is

00:06:29.708 --> 00:06:30.562
actually appropriate.

00:06:30.626 --> 00:06:33.846
Perchta can appear as either a beautiful goddess who appears as white as snow,

00:06:33.868 --> 00:06:37.186
or an ugly, haggard old woman, a lot like the evil queen from Snow White.

00:06:37.218 --> 00:06:39.702
Perchta would team up with Krampus many years later.

00:06:39.756 --> 00:06:41.742
So I'll go deeper into her lore in a little bit.

00:06:41.796 --> 00:06:45.246
Krampuslauf became a long standing tradition, primarily in Austria and Germany,

00:06:45.268 --> 00:06:47.962
which has come back in a major way over the last decade.

00:06:48.026 --> 00:06:49.550
My first thought was, this is awesome.

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:52.366
Why don't we have this in the west? But after doing a little digging,

00:06:52.388 --> 00:06:54.590
there are some recent Krampus parades in U.S. cities.

00:06:54.670 --> 00:06:57.874
However, much like our music festivals, they are way tamer than their

00:06:57.912 --> 00:06:59.070
European counterparts.

00:06:59.150 --> 00:07:00.606
One might even say that they are...

00:07:01.753 --> 00:07:02.920
- VERY BAD!

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:06.130
Meanwhile, in Austria, you've got stuff like this going on.

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:09.846
-[Amyscrypt] I got attacked and pulled down, and so did a lot of other people.

00:07:09.948 --> 00:07:12.194
-[Amyscrypt] They were attacking kids, they were attacking the elderly.

00:07:12.242 --> 00:07:13.362
-[Amyscrypt] No one was really safe.

00:07:13.426 --> 00:07:16.854
And isn't that what Christmas is really all about? But the survival of these

00:07:16.892 --> 00:07:18.674
celebrations was not without pushback.

00:07:18.722 --> 00:07:21.878
The Catholic Church attempted to ban any celebration of Krampus in the

00:07:21.884 --> 00:07:24.618
1100s due to the creature's resemblance to their concept of the devil,

00:07:24.624 --> 00:07:27.786
which clearly demonstrates that they believed in him and feared him

00:07:27.808 --> 00:07:29.494
enough to want to bring down the ban hammer.

00:07:29.542 --> 00:07:30.586
And that's pretty great.

00:07:30.688 --> 00:07:33.151
Over time, the celebration of St. Nicholas Feast Day

00:07:33.151 --> 00:07:35.050
became intertwined with Christmas celebrations,

00:07:35.130 --> 00:07:36.442
especially in European countries.

00:07:36.506 --> 00:07:38.734
And since Krampus is the dark counterpart to St. Nick, 

00:07:38.772 --> 00:07:42.893
it too became associated with the birthday party of the world's most famous zombie.

00:07:42.893 --> 00:07:45.306
Much to the annoyance of the Catholic Church,

00:07:45.338 --> 00:07:47.014
who was unable to stomp out the legend with their bans.

00:07:47.082 --> 00:07:50.418
Maybe The Streisand Effect, the phenomenon of attempted censorship of a topic

00:07:50.424 --> 00:07:53.394
inadvertently increasing awareness about that subject,

00:07:53.432 --> 00:07:55.186
should actually be called The Krampus Effect.

00:07:55.288 --> 00:07:58.334
The character managed to survive until the 1890s, where a new holiday

00:07:58.382 --> 00:07:59.270
tradition took place.

00:07:59.340 --> 00:08:02.434
Krampuskarten literally just translates to Krampus Cards.

00:08:02.482 --> 00:08:05.638
These holiday cards showed the December demon in a series of snapshots where

00:08:05.644 --> 00:08:08.486
he is kidnapping various children, and it allowed word of his power to

00:08:08.508 --> 00:08:11.410
spread around the world like never before, using the postal service.

00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:14.726
This is another interesting, perhaps coincidental, parallel that Krampus

00:08:14.758 --> 00:08:15.542
shares with Sam.

00:08:15.606 --> 00:08:18.774
Sam's legend was spread early on, thanks to a series of

00:08:18.822 --> 00:08:20.390
Halloween greeting cards created by Michael Dougherty.

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:24.067
So make sure to send your family and friends a Krampuskarten this holiday season.

00:08:24.067 --> 00:08:26.766
But I guess the increased awareness about Krampus was not enough to

00:08:26.788 --> 00:08:27.722
deter bad behavior

00:08:27.786 --> 00:08:30.542
In one village in Austria during the 1930s.

00:08:30.596 --> 00:08:33.326
This was in the middle of a great depression for the country, and food was

00:08:33.348 --> 00:08:34.014
hard to come by.

00:08:34.052 --> 00:08:36.986
A little girl standing in a breadline was rushed by a crowd of desperate,

00:08:37.018 --> 00:08:39.642
hungry people who stole her bread and shoved her to the ground.

00:08:39.706 --> 00:08:42.586
When she arrived home, her parents were angry at her for coming up empty handed.

00:08:42.618 --> 00:08:45.458
And when she tried to show some optimism by presenting her Santa Claus doll,

00:08:45.474 --> 00:08:48.374
her parents ripped it in half, causing her to lose her true

00:08:48.412 --> 00:08:51.106
Christmas spirit and chuck the toy into the fireplace.

00:08:51.298 --> 00:08:53.606
-[Omi] They too had given up.

00:08:53.708 --> 00:08:56.182
-[Omi] And eventually, so did I.

00:08:56.316 --> 00:09:00.086
-[Omi] And for the first time, I didn't wish for a miracle.

00:09:00.198 --> 00:09:02.602
-[Omi] I wished for them to go away.

00:09:02.736 --> 00:09:05.654
-[Omi] A wish I would come to regret.

00:09:05.782 --> 00:09:12.294
-[Omi] And that night, in the darkness of a howling blizzard, I got my wish.

00:09:12.422 --> 00:09:15.778
There's a reason I've been pointing out all of Krampus's similarities to Sam

00:09:15.814 --> 00:09:16.670
throughout this video.

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:20.834
And that's because by the time of Mike Dougherty's take on Krampus in the 2015 film,

00:09:20.834 --> 00:09:23.434
Krampus's role in the story has been expanded not just to punish

00:09:23.482 --> 00:09:26.506
naughty children, but to punish anyone who has lost sight of the true spirit

00:09:26.538 --> 00:09:27.130
of the holiday.

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:31.117
In that sense, he becomes a lot more like Sam, but for Christmas instead of Halloween.

00:09:31.117 --> 00:09:33.474
Although there is no rule that says Sam can't come out around Christmas time,

00:09:33.512 --> 00:09:35.646
and he does, maybe Sam vs. Kram

00:09:35.678 --> 00:09:37.138
is somewhere in our future.

00:09:37.224 --> 00:09:40.190
Narratively, for Krampus, this could be seen as him getting stricter with

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:41.190
his rules over time.

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:44.326
At first, he gets people's attention by kidnapping naughty kids, but then he

00:09:44.348 --> 00:09:47.318
expands out to include adults and anyone who disrespects the rules of the holiday.

00:09:47.324 --> 00:09:50.674
So those who fail to uphold the tenets of celebration, generosity,

00:09:50.722 --> 00:09:52.162
and tradition become victims.

00:09:52.226 --> 00:09:55.398
To put this in Death Note terms, it kind of follows the pattern of how Kira

00:09:55.414 --> 00:09:58.438
started out by only killing criminals, but eventually expanded to include

00:09:58.454 --> 00:10:01.434
those who did things that are not crimes but could also hurt others.

00:10:01.552 --> 00:10:04.750
We can also see how Krampus has evolved with the times in order to continue

00:10:04.820 --> 00:10:06.126
mirroring his lighter half, St. Nicholas.

00:10:06.148 --> 00:10:07.086
Old St. Nick had undergone

00:10:07.108 --> 00:10:09.530
some changes in the late modern period.

00:10:09.610 --> 00:10:12.642
Dutch settlers brought the celebration of St. Nicholas to America,

00:10:12.642 --> 00:10:14.634
calling him Sinterklaas, which was eventually

00:10:14.682 --> 00:10:16.362
Americanized to Santa Claus.

00:10:16.426 --> 00:10:19.166
It seems that his waistline was also Americanized.

00:10:19.278 --> 00:10:22.626
As he got more popular, he enlisted the help of some elves to accelerate the

00:10:22.648 --> 00:10:23.538
toy making process.

00:10:23.624 --> 00:10:25.710
These would be known as Santa's Little Helpers.

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:27.842
So Krampus got some minions of his own.

00:10:27.896 --> 00:10:31.414
But true to his nature, Krampus's helpers were demonic looking versions of

00:10:31.452 --> 00:10:34.242
symbols and objects typically associated with Christmas cheer.

00:10:34.306 --> 00:10:37.558
They included a trio of mischievous gingerbread man: Lumpy, Dumpy, and Clumpy.

00:10:37.564 --> 00:10:40.866
As well as an army of evil toys, such as the monstrous and hungry

00:10:40.898 --> 00:10:45.000
jack in the box known as Der Clown, a bloodthirsty teddy bear known as Teddy Klaue

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:47.270
and a rogue robot toy known as Tik Tok.

00:10:47.350 --> 00:10:50.746
Unlike my M3GAN Horror History episode, this is not some kind of

00:10:50.768 --> 00:10:53.734
allegory about how the app TikTok is corrupting the minds of the youth

00:10:53.782 --> 00:10:55.470
because TikTok didn't even exist yet.

00:10:55.540 --> 00:10:58.894
There's also an evil angel puppet named Perchta who seems to be another form

00:10:58.932 --> 00:11:00.618
of the Christmas witch Frau Perchta

00:11:00.634 --> 00:11:03.982
Seen during the Krampuslauf runs, Frau Perchta would come around after

00:11:04.036 --> 00:11:07.194
Christmas time each year to punish those who neglect their household duties,

00:11:07.242 --> 00:11:09.582
primarily women who didn't get all their flax spinning done.

00:11:09.636 --> 00:11:12.362
She would come to your house and set fires to the half spun fiber.

00:11:12.426 --> 00:11:15.030
If your house was messy when she arrived or you didn't leave out a

00:11:15.060 --> 00:11:18.262
traditional bowl of porridge for her, she was said to slit your stomach open

00:11:18.316 --> 00:11:21.974
with a long knife hidden under her robes, disembowel you in your sleep, and

00:11:22.012 --> 00:11:24.082
replace your guts with rocks and straw.

00:11:24.146 --> 00:11:26.886
Now you understand why people dress up as her to try to scare kids during

00:11:26.908 --> 00:11:28.022
the Krampuslauf Runs,

00:11:28.076 --> 00:11:30.050
This chick is one bad witch.

00:11:30.130 --> 00:11:31.322
I was gonna say something else.

00:11:31.376 --> 00:11:34.486
In addition to all of those layers, Krampus also worked with a team of troll

00:11:34.518 --> 00:11:37.686
like creatures called Yule Lads, which each played a role in terrorizing

00:11:37.718 --> 00:11:39.130
Krampus's victim.

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:42.756
(IMPACT)

00:11:44.329 --> 00:11:48.267
♪ Mysterious Music ♪

00:11:48.267 --> 00:11:51.498
The Yule Lads originated from Icelandic Christmas folklore,

00:11:51.514 --> 00:11:54.382
mountain dwelling monsters who came down into town around Christmas to eat

00:11:54.436 --> 00:11:55.534
disobedient children.

00:11:55.652 --> 00:11:58.546
Traditionally, each of them is associated with a different prank with

00:11:58.568 --> 00:11:59.902
varying levels of severity.

00:11:59.966 --> 00:12:03.278
They include Ketkrókur, the meat hook, because he was known for

00:12:03.294 --> 00:12:04.030
snatching human meat.

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:05.742
Þvörusleikir, the Spoon Licker;

00:12:05.806 --> 00:12:09.342
Huroaskellir, the door slammer, who gets a joy out of making people grumpy;

00:12:09.406 --> 00:12:12.918
Kertasníkir, the candle beggar, who eats candles, leaving his victims in the dark;

00:12:12.924 --> 00:12:16.486
Gáttaþefur, the doorway sniffer, who can smell baked goods and

00:12:16.508 --> 00:12:17.650
steals bread and cookies;

00:12:17.730 --> 00:12:20.850
Bjúgnakrækir, the sausage swiper, who steals smoked meat.

00:12:20.930 --> 00:12:24.586
Giljagaur, the gully gawk, who puts a potato in your shoe, which is a very

00:12:24.608 --> 00:12:26.810
minor inconvenience compared to the meat hook guy.

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:30.522
Gluggagægir, the window peeper, who's essentially Krampus's spy and

00:12:30.576 --> 00:12:33.998
Stekkjarstaur, the sheep harasser, who steals sheep's milk and also leaves a potato,

00:12:34.004 --> 00:12:36.974
which could be a good thing if you like potatoes more than you like milk.

00:12:37.012 --> 00:12:40.414
However, while working under Krampus, the Yule Lads take on much

00:12:40.452 --> 00:12:41.722
darker intentions.

00:12:41.866 --> 00:12:43.730
-[Omi] He and his helpers.

00:12:46.310 --> 00:12:53.070
-[Omi] I could only listen as they dragged my family into the underworld

00:12:53.230 --> 00:12:55.638
-[Omi] knowing that I would be next.

00:12:55.804 --> 00:12:59.910
-[Omi] But Krampus didn't take me that night.

00:13:00.060 --> 00:13:06.792
-[Omi] He left me as a reminder of what happens when hope is lost,

00:13:06.792 --> 00:13:11.218
-[Omi] when belief is forgotten and the Christmas spirit dies.

00:13:11.314 --> 00:13:14.474
The little girl is given a bell with Krampus's name on it to remember what

00:13:14.512 --> 00:13:15.210
happened that night.

00:13:15.280 --> 00:13:18.522
Many decades later, in the 2010s, that girl has a family of her own,

00:13:18.576 --> 00:13:22.298
including her son Tom, her daughter in law Sarah, and two grandkids, Max and Beth,

00:13:22.304 --> 00:13:25.302
who refer to her as Omi, the German word for grandmother.

00:13:25.366 --> 00:13:27.710
After so many years, Omi thought she was in the clear.

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:30.766
But this year, maybe the first year that Max is old enough to grapple with

00:13:30.788 --> 00:13:34.026
the idea of Santa Claus possibly being a fallacy;

00:13:34.058 --> 00:13:35.470
the family's Christmas spirit is at an all time low.

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:39.106
Max gets into a fight at a nativity recital at the local Mucho Mart

00:13:39.128 --> 00:13:40.562
While his sister laughs and records him.

00:13:40.616 --> 00:13:43.006
This is the bad behavior that catches Krampus's eye.

00:13:43.038 --> 00:13:46.446
But the evil Xmas entity would take notice of the entire family when Max's

00:13:46.478 --> 00:13:49.038
letter to Santa is exposed by the visiting cousins.

00:13:49.134 --> 00:13:50.966
-[Max] I just wanted Christmas to be like it used to be.

00:13:50.988 --> 00:13:51.798
-[Max] But forget it.

00:13:51.884 --> 00:13:52.978
-[Max] I hate Christmas.

00:13:53.074 --> 00:13:54.022
-[Max] I hate all of you.

00:13:54.076 --> 00:13:57.222
Which is actually still not as bad as what Kevin McAllister told his family

00:13:57.276 --> 00:13:58.178
in Home Alone.

00:13:58.274 --> 00:14:00.742
-[Kevin] I don't want to see you again for the rest of my whole life.

00:14:00.796 --> 00:14:02.966
-[Kevin] I hope I never see any jerks again.

00:14:03.068 --> 00:14:05.786
Maybe if Krampus had been the one to break into his house, he would have had

00:14:05.808 --> 00:14:08.070
more success than the duo of bumbling burglars.

00:14:08.150 --> 00:14:11.334
Anyway. Max tears up his letter to Santa, and it's sucked into a whirlwind.

00:14:11.382 --> 00:14:14.530
It's almost as if releasing this letter into the night's air is a catalyst

00:14:14.550 --> 00:14:17.326
for the blizzard that immediately rolls in, knocks out the power, and

00:14:17.348 --> 00:14:19.978
deadlocks the family in place together in their own neighborhood.

00:14:20.074 --> 00:14:23.934
The next morning, December 23rd, Max notices a creepy snowman in the front lawn

00:14:23.972 --> 00:14:27.158
almost spying on them, and they receive a couple of unmarked

00:14:27.194 --> 00:14:28.350
Christmas presents at their doorstep.

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:31.826
The neighborhood seems like it's almost entirely empty as Beth walks down

00:14:31.848 --> 00:14:33.134
the block to visit her boyfriend.

00:14:33.182 --> 00:14:37.202
But on the way there, the sky goes dark and she hears sleigh bells overhead.

00:14:37.266 --> 00:14:40.520
But this is not the Christmas legend that she is familiar with.

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:45.396
(THUD) (breath trembling) (creature growls)

00:14:45.551 --> 00:14:46.491
–[Beth] Oh my God…

00:14:51.224 --> 00:14:52.910
(SCREAMING)

00:14:52.910 --> 00:14:56.438
Beth tries to escape to a parcel delivery van, but finds the driver frozen

00:14:56.454 --> 00:14:58.794
to death inside, so she hides out underneath it.

00:14:58.832 --> 00:15:01.206
We pretty much know what all the family members did to provoke Krampus's wrath,

00:15:01.238 --> 00:15:04.614
But what did this delivery driver do? He seemed innocent enough,

00:15:04.662 --> 00:15:07.370
like he even braved the awful weather to deliver their package.

00:15:07.450 --> 00:15:10.078
Most delivery drivers would have just dumped it in the sewer and marked it

00:15:10.084 --> 00:15:10.810
as delivered.

00:15:10.890 --> 00:15:11.758
– [Bender] Too much work.

00:15:11.844 --> 00:15:14.166
Let's burn it and say we dumped it in the sewer.

00:15:14.218 --> 00:15:17.586
Whatever happened to respect for essential workers? In any event, Beth seems

00:15:17.608 --> 00:15:21.679
to be in the clear, until she notices that Krampus has left behind a little present.

00:15:23.452 --> 00:15:24.701
(SCREAMING)

00:15:24.701 --> 00:15:27.326
Back at the house, another ominous snowman has appeared.

00:15:27.358 --> 00:15:30.286
And that evening, Tom and Uncle Howard discover hooved footprints

00:15:30.318 --> 00:15:33.606
while out looking for Beth, Howard is attacked by a creature burrowing under

00:15:33.628 --> 00:15:36.190
the snow and nearly pulled into the ground right then and there,

00:15:36.190 --> 00:15:37.478
presumably to take him to hell.

00:15:37.478 --> 00:15:40.162
Tom is able to save him, but the bite wounds are severe.

00:15:40.226 --> 00:15:42.674
Fans tend to refer to this creature as the Snow Beast.

00:15:42.722 --> 00:15:45.514
It's hard to tell exactly what it is because it's never seen, but it seems

00:15:45.552 --> 00:15:48.326
to operate similar to the Graboid from the Tremors franchise.

00:15:48.438 --> 00:15:51.594
That night, as the family drifts off to sleep around the fireplace, their

00:15:51.632 --> 00:15:54.586
only source of warmth, the flame dwindles down, allowing one of the

00:15:54.608 --> 00:15:57.546
gingerbread men to descend to the chimney on a metal chain and abduct

00:15:57.578 --> 00:15:58.986
Howard's son, Howie Jr.

00:15:59.098 --> 00:16:02.266
This happens right after the battery dies on an iPad that had been playing

00:16:02.298 --> 00:16:03.038
Christmas music.

00:16:03.124 --> 00:16:06.138
It kind of makes me wonder if that needed to happen before the evil

00:16:06.154 --> 00:16:07.454
gingerbread man could attack.

00:16:07.572 --> 00:16:10.466
Considering how many characters in Trick r Treat become vulnerable the moment

00:16:10.488 --> 00:16:13.486
that they ruined a Halloween tradition, it could be that the warm fire

00:16:13.518 --> 00:16:16.626
and Christmas music were the things protecting the family until they

00:16:16.648 --> 00:16:17.410
both went out.

00:16:17.480 --> 00:16:20.366
It brings to mind Macy, who became the target of a horde of dead

00:16:20.398 --> 00:16:23.330
schoolchildren the moment that she extinguished the final Jack o Lantern.

00:16:23.410 --> 00:16:26.246
Beth was punished for choosing boyfriend over family and leaving them.

00:16:26.268 --> 00:16:27.282
And now Howie Jr.

00:16:27.346 --> 00:16:29.862
Happened to be the closest victim when the flame and music went out.

00:16:29.916 --> 00:16:32.646
Or maybe it has something to do with him trying to take a bite out of the

00:16:32.668 --> 00:16:33.382
gingerbread man.

00:16:33.436 --> 00:16:34.754
Like, you're not supposed to eat the cookies.

00:16:34.802 --> 00:16:36.194
You're supposed to leave them out for Santa.

00:16:36.242 --> 00:16:39.042
But to be fair, that gingerbread man was kind of begging to be eaten.

00:16:39.106 --> 00:16:41.082
The family is unable able to save Howie Jr.

00:16:41.146 --> 00:16:43.038
Practically burning the house down in the process.

00:16:43.124 --> 00:16:47.466
As the clock rolls over to December 24th, Christmas Eve, Omi explains to Max's cousins,

00:16:47.498 --> 00:16:50.654
Stevie and Jordan that Krampus judges them not just on their behavior,

00:16:50.692 --> 00:16:53.338
but also by what they believe in their hearts.

00:16:53.434 --> 00:16:56.478
As the two of them head to the upstairs bathroom, they're attacked by the

00:16:56.484 --> 00:16:59.454
contents of the unmarked packages that Krampus left for them the previous day.

00:16:59.502 --> 00:17:03.234
Jordan is devoured by Der Klown, who seems to have grown larger since

00:17:03.272 --> 00:17:06.614
abducting Beth, but the adults are able to save Stevie and fend it off, only

00:17:06.652 --> 00:17:09.670
to come face to unsettling face with Perchta.

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:12.604
(shrieking) (all screaming) (shrieks)

00:17:12.604 --> 00:17:14.604
(IMPACT)

00:17:17.273 --> 00:17:21.040
♪ Holiday Music ♪

00:17:21.040 --> 00:17:24.618
The adults in the attic not only have to pry Perchta from off of Sarah, but

00:17:24.624 --> 00:17:28.214
they're charged by Teddy Klaue and continually jabbed by the robot Tik Tok.

00:17:28.262 --> 00:17:30.106
That name still sounds weird every time I say it now.

00:17:30.128 --> 00:17:33.430
Downstairs, the gingerbread trio stages an attack on Howard,

00:17:33.440 --> 00:17:35.150
who is able to fend them off with the help of his dog.

00:17:35.220 --> 00:17:38.270
But when the family reconvenes in the living room, something can be heard

00:17:38.340 --> 00:17:39.950
skulking above the ceiling.

00:17:39.950 --> 00:17:41.730
(creatures growling)

00:17:41.730 --> 00:17:45.098
Der Klown falls through from above, and another massive battle with the army

00:17:45.114 --> 00:17:46.010
of toys ensues.

00:17:46.090 --> 00:17:49.258
But before Aunt Dorothy can fire off the finishing shot, the family finds out

00:17:49.274 --> 00:17:53.192
just what was hiding in those creepy snowmen that have been piling up outside the house. 

00:17:53.360 --> 00:17:54.428
-[Omi] Elves.

00:17:54.530 --> 00:17:56.642
These are the Yule Lads that I mentioned earlier.

00:17:56.706 --> 00:17:59.030
Once they break through the wall, it's pretty much game over.

00:17:59.100 --> 00:18:00.354
One of them steals the baby.

00:18:00.402 --> 00:18:04.457
Then Aunt Dorothy and Uncle Howard are yanked out of the house via chain not long after

00:18:04.457 --> 00:18:07.407
realizing that they'll have to ditch the house in order to have any chance to survive,

00:18:07.407 --> 00:18:10.288
they make a break for the broken down snowplow out on the street,

00:18:10.288 --> 00:18:12.266
but Omi stays back to finish what she started with

00:18:12.288 --> 00:18:13.978
Krampus all of those years ago.

00:18:14.064 --> 00:18:17.930
Everyone knows that old Saint Nick comes down the chimney to give, that is,

00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:19.306
give presents to children.

00:18:19.408 --> 00:18:22.858
So you'd expect that his opposite half would come down the chimney and take.

00:18:22.944 --> 00:18:24.410
And that's exactly what he does.

00:18:24.480 --> 00:18:27.754
Take the life of the girl who it had given a warning to so many decades before.

00:18:27.802 --> 00:18:31.358
Who needs Santa Claus when this fabled bringer of fear possesses a

00:18:31.364 --> 00:18:35.006
huge pair of actual claws to open up his satchel of tricks and let the evil

00:18:35.038 --> 00:18:37.186
toys within pounce on the old woman.

00:18:40.151 --> 00:18:43.854
Outside Max watches as his family is picked off one by one by The Snow Beast,

00:18:43.902 --> 00:18:46.466
burrowing around under the icy powder, proving that it would have been

00:18:46.488 --> 00:18:48.098
impossible to escape at any point.

00:18:48.184 --> 00:18:51.606
Only he and Stevie make it to the snowplow, and when the elves abduct her,

00:18:51.628 --> 00:18:54.706
he finally finds himself face to face with Krampus.

00:18:54.818 --> 00:18:58.006
An interesting detail here is that when he finally gets a good look at the

00:18:58.028 --> 00:19:00.886
creature that's been haunting his family, it doesn't seem to present its

00:19:00.908 --> 00:19:01.614
true face.

00:19:01.682 --> 00:19:05.210
It's almost as if it's wearing the skin of an old man, resembling something

00:19:05.280 --> 00:19:07.622
a little bit closer to the traditional Santa Claus.

00:19:07.686 --> 00:19:11.066
Director Michael Dougherty may have indirectly addressed this in a 2022

00:19:11.088 --> 00:19:13.642
interview with Slash Film: We wanted to go with something that looked ancient,

00:19:13.696 --> 00:19:16.426
you know, something that looked like it walked out of the dark ages

00:19:16.458 --> 00:19:16.990
in a sense.

00:19:17.060 --> 00:19:19.674
The fur pelts, the heavy coats, the rusty chains.

00:19:19.722 --> 00:19:22.874
But we also wanted to acknowledge that everybody's interpretation of Krampus

00:19:22.922 --> 00:19:23.438
is different.

00:19:23.524 --> 00:19:26.570
So we like the idea that we never fully reveal Krampus.

00:19:26.650 --> 00:19:30.626
You see a face, but is that his real face or not? Krampus gives Max his

00:19:30.648 --> 00:19:33.806
ripped up letter back, making it clear that it was his wish that triggered

00:19:33.838 --> 00:19:34.370
all of this.

00:19:34.440 --> 00:19:38.146
He realizes he is now the one being left alive to tell the tale to a new generation.

00:19:38.168 --> 00:19:41.954
Max receives the same bell that was once given to Omi to remind

00:19:42.002 --> 00:19:43.810
her not to take the holiday for granted.

00:19:43.890 --> 00:19:47.046
But before the sleigh and the horrible creatures that came on it take off

00:19:47.068 --> 00:19:47.670
into the night.

00:19:47.740 --> 00:19:51.326
Max comes upon it and sees one more frightful twist on the Christmas stories

00:19:51.378 --> 00:19:52.458
that he's accustomed to.

00:19:52.544 --> 00:19:55.894
Most cliche Christmas movies have a scene where someone hears Santa Claus

00:19:55.942 --> 00:19:57.382
landing on the roof with his reindeer.

00:19:57.446 --> 00:19:59.462
But those do not sound like reindeer.

00:19:59.526 --> 00:20:03.478
Krampus, as usual, has his own twisted variant known as Yule Goats.

00:20:03.574 --> 00:20:06.426
Like many of the creatures that assist him during the Christmas season,

00:20:06.458 --> 00:20:08.442
Yule Goats have ties to ancient Pagan religion.

00:20:08.506 --> 00:20:11.534
Thor, the Norse God of thunder, was said to have a chariot pulled by these

00:20:11.572 --> 00:20:12.378
magic goats.

00:20:12.474 --> 00:20:15.486
But just like with Krampus, the Christian church feared these creatures and

00:20:15.508 --> 00:20:16.682
declared them as demonic.

00:20:16.746 --> 00:20:20.306
Tales were spread of the demonic Yule Goats roaming Scandinavia for food and

00:20:20.328 --> 00:20:21.074
scaring children.

00:20:21.192 --> 00:20:23.726
Like some of the others, the Yule Goat is still a part of some Nordic

00:20:23.758 --> 00:20:27.134
Christmas celebrations today, most notably in Sweden, in the form of a giant

00:20:27.182 --> 00:20:30.374
decorative goat made of straw that pranksters like to try to burn down every year.

00:20:30.412 --> 00:20:33.826
The Yule Goats pulling Krampus's sleigh are huge, aggressive monsters

00:20:33.858 --> 00:20:36.898
with black fur, ram like horns, and an intimidating roar.

00:20:36.994 --> 00:20:39.978
By the way, listen to the music being played by the Yule Lads right here as

00:20:39.984 --> 00:20:41.340
they prepare to take off.

00:20:41.340 --> 00:20:47.150
♪ Traditional Krampuslauf Music ♪

00:20:47.150 --> 00:20:50.506
It sounds a lot like the traditional Krampuslauf music that I

00:20:50.538 --> 00:20:51.310
played earlier.

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:56.187
♪ Traditional Krampuslauf Music ♪

00:20:56.290 --> 00:20:59.134
That's a very cool detail that I never would have noticed had I not made

00:20:59.172 --> 00:20:59.678
this video.

00:20:59.764 --> 00:21:03.038
Max finds the elves restraining his cousin Stevie, and in the last push of

00:21:03.044 --> 00:21:06.494
desperation tries taking back his wish and asking that he be taken instead

00:21:06.532 --> 00:21:07.198
of his family.

00:21:07.284 --> 00:21:10.718
He throws the Krampus bell and in the spot it landed in the ground cracks

00:21:10.734 --> 00:21:13.250
and opens up a huge fissure leading straight to hell.

00:21:13.320 --> 00:21:16.642
It seems that he's finally going to make good on the old stories of the

00:21:16.696 --> 00:21:21.067
Half goat, half demon that drags misbehaving kids to an appointment with Satan himself.

00:21:21.067 --> 00:21:23.686
When Max realizes that Stevie is gonna be thrown into the pit for

00:21:23.708 --> 00:21:26.934
his own transgression, he begs the malefic entity to please take him instead.

00:21:26.972 --> 00:21:30.474
After touching a cold claw to the child's tears, it seems that

00:21:30.512 --> 00:21:33.562
maybe Max has learned his lesson, and the horned hell bringer may actually

00:21:33.616 --> 00:21:34.298
back down.

00:21:34.384 --> 00:21:35.980
But then this happens.

00:21:35.980 --> 00:21:38.350
(Krampus laughter)

00:21:38.350 --> 00:21:40.650
The child's misery is amusing to them.

00:21:40.720 --> 00:21:44.201
There is no redemption when it comes to Christmas wishes as it turns out.

00:21:44.201 --> 00:21:46.974
Stevie is hurled into the pit, and Max follows not long after.

00:21:47.012 --> 00:21:51.246
But somehow, Max wakes up the next day, Christmas morning, almost as

00:21:51.268 --> 00:21:53.722
if the horror of the last two days was only a dream.

00:21:53.786 --> 00:21:57.038
He comes downstairs for presents with his family, who are all alive.

00:21:57.134 --> 00:22:01.330
But something seems off, and Max realizes it when he opens one present

00:22:01.400 --> 00:22:04.606
containing the Krampus bell, causing everyone to realize that the nightmare

00:22:04.638 --> 00:22:06.862
that they thought they had awoken from was reality.

00:22:06.926 --> 00:22:08.782
A glance out the window reveals the truth.

00:22:08.846 --> 00:22:11.718
They've been captured inside one of the creature's many snow globes, in a

00:22:11.724 --> 00:22:14.694
room filled with the many families that he's punished over thousands of years.

00:22:14.732 --> 00:22:17.702
The message when it comes to Krampus is a simple one.

00:22:17.756 --> 00:22:20.886
You better watch out, because ending up on the naughty list is easier than

00:22:20.908 --> 00:22:23.898
you might think, and the consequences are much worse than you'd expect.

00:22:23.984 --> 00:22:27.146
An eternity of suffering in a personal hell, stuck inside a house with

00:22:27.168 --> 00:22:30.010
family members you can barely stand to spend three days with every year.

00:22:30.080 --> 00:22:33.818
Like Sam, Krampus is not necessarily a villain, but rather an enforcer of

00:22:33.824 --> 00:22:34.662
holiday tradition.

00:22:34.726 --> 00:22:37.022
If you don't break the rules, he won't be a problem for you.

00:22:37.076 --> 00:22:38.394
Except for the delivery driver.

00:22:38.442 --> 00:22:39.802
That guy was just unlucky.

00:22:39.866 --> 00:22:41.594
And now that I think about it, the baby.

00:22:41.642 --> 00:22:44.538
What could the baby have done to deserve eternity in hell?

00:22:44.554 --> 00:22:46.842
And why wasn't the delivery driver there with them in the snow globe?

00:22:46.842 --> 00:22:47.680
So many questions.

00:22:47.680 --> 00:22:50.547
Over the years, we've seen Krampus adapt with the times,

00:22:50.547 --> 00:22:53.534
surviving religious bands and merging with other holidays to stay relevant.

00:22:53.582 --> 00:22:57.924
Through postcards, storytelling, traditional parades and festivals, and now movies.

00:22:57.924 --> 00:23:00.566
Krampus seems to be more popular than ever, thanks to a boom of

00:23:00.588 --> 00:23:03.442
Krampus movies in the 2010s, including Rare Exports,

00:23:03.506 --> 00:23:04.866
Krampus: the Christmas Devil,

00:23:04.898 --> 00:23:05.954
Krampus: The Reckoning,

